    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Example problem: maximum sum of any k consecutive values.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nfunction maxFixedWindowSum(\n  nums: readonly number[],\n  k: number,\n): number | null {\n  if (k <= 0 || k > nums.length) return null;\n\n  let windowSum = 0;\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n    windowSum += nums[i]!;\n  }\n\n  let best = windowSum;\n\n  for (let right = k; right < nums.length; right++) {\n    windowSum += nums[right]!;\n    windowSum -= nums[right - k]!;\n    best = Math.max(best, windowSum);\n  }\n\n  return best;\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction maxFixedWindowSumUsingReduce(\n  nums: readonly number[],\n  k: number,\n): number | null {\n  if (k <= 0 || k > nums.length) return null;\n\n  let best = -Infinity;\n\n  for (let i = 0; i + k <= nums.length; i++) {\n    const sum = nums.slice(i, i + k)\n      .reduce((total, value) => total + value, 0);\n\n    best = Math.max(best, sum);\n  }\n\n  return best;\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Example:\n[2,1,5,1,3,2], k=3\nwindows:\n[2,1,5] = 8\n[1,5,1] = 7\n[5,1,3] = 9\n[1,3,2] = 6\nanswer = 9.\n\nStep 3 — Complexity:\nCore sliding window = O(n) time, O(1) auxiliary space.\nBuilt-in slice/reduce baseline = O(nk).",
