    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Maintain a fixed-size ring buffer and rolling sum.\n\nWITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE:\n```ts\nclass RollingAverage {\n  private readonly buffer: number[];\n  private count = 0;\n  private position = 0;\n  private sum = 0;\n\n  constructor(private readonly size: number) {\n    if (size <= 0) throw new Error(\"size must be positive\");\n    this.buffer = new Array<number>(size).fill(0);\n  }\n\n  add(value: number): number {\n    if (this.count < this.size) {\n      this.buffer[this.position] = value;\n      this.sum += value;\n      this.count++;\n    } else {\n      this.sum -= this.buffer[this.position]!;\n      this.buffer[this.position] = value;\n      this.sum += value;\n    }\n\n    this.position = (this.position + 1) % this.size;\n    return this.sum / this.count;\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWITH BUILT-IN:\n```ts\nfunction rollingAverages(\n  values: readonly number[],\n  size: number,\n): number[] {\n  if (size <= 0) return [];\n\n  const result: number[] = [];\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {\n    const start = Math.max(0, i - size + 1);\n    const window = values.slice(start, i + 1);\n\n    result.push(\n      window.reduce((sum, value) => sum + value, 0) / window.length,\n    );\n  }\n\n  return result;\n}\n```\n\nStep 2 — Example:\nsize=3, values 1,2,3,4\naverages: 1, 1.5, 2, 3.\n\nStep 3 — Complexity:\nRing-buffer update O(1) per event, O(k) memory.\nBuilt-in baseline O(nk) time.",
