    deepExplanation: "Step 1 — Recognition checklist:\n1. Is the problem about a contiguous subarray/substring or recent events?\n2. Is there a fixed k, or does the window expand/shrink by a constraint?\n3. Can the state be updated by adding the new right item and removing the old left item?\n4. Is the validity predicate monotonic when the left pointer moves?\n5. Can each pointer move only forward?\n\nStep 2 — WITHOUT BUILT-IN / CORE template:\n```ts\nfunction slidingWindowTemplate(\n  values: readonly number[],\n  isInvalid: (sum: number) => boolean,\n): number {\n  let left = 0;\n  let sum = 0;\n  let best = 0;\n\n  for (let right = 0; right < values.length; right++) {\n    sum += values[right]!;\n\n    while (isInvalid(sum)) {\n      sum -= values[left]!;\n      left++;\n    }\n\n    best = Math.max(best, right - left + 1);\n  }\n\n  return best;\n}\n```\n\nStep 3 — WITH BUILT-IN-style baseline:\n```ts\nfunction bruteForceWindowLength(\n  values: readonly number[],\n  predicate: (window: number[]) => boolean,\n): number {\n  let best = 0;\n\n  for (let start = 0; start < values.length; start++) {\n    for (let end = start + 1; end <= values.length; end++) {\n      if (predicate([...values.slice(start, end)])) {\n        best = Math.max(best, end - start);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  return best;\n}\n```\n\nStep 4 — Recognition warning:\nNot every contiguous-subarray problem is a sliding window. Maximum subarray sum with arbitrary negative values is better expressed using Kadane's algorithm; problems with non-monotonic constraints may require prefix sums, binary search, DP, heaps, or other tools.\n\nComplexity target:\nTwo-pointer sliding-window scans are usually O(n) when each pointer advances at most n times.",
